acceptanceCriteria.text:
Screenshots show:
- a two-hunk diff with line numbers, additions and deletions;
- the no-newline marker;
- a CRLF file without visible carriage returns;
- the binary message;
- the 5,000-line change showing 2,000 lines with Show more.

`readWorkingDiff` returns:
- text hunks with old and new line numbers for tracked and untracked files;
- `binary` for binary files;
- `too_large` above the limit;
- `empty` for a mode-only change.

Tests cover each, plus a file without a final newline and a CRLF file whose lines keep their `\r`.

tickets.body:
Size: **medium**. This ticket reads what Source control shows: the repository state and one file's diff. It requires the runner (`src/main/git/runner.ts`).

**Shared types** (`src/shared/git/status.ts`, `src/shared/git/diff.ts`; renderer-safe, with no Node imports)
```ts
export type FileChangeKind = 'added' | 'modified' | 'deleted' | 'renamed' | 'copied' | 'typechange' | 'untracked' | 'conflicted'
export interface FileChange { path: string; oldPath: string | null; kind: FileChangeKind }
export interface BranchState { name: string | null /* null when detached */; headOid: string | null /* null on an unborn branch */; upstream: string | null; ahead: number; behind: number }
export type OperationInProgress = 'merge' | 'rebase' | 'cherry-pick' | 'revert' | null
export interface RepoStatus { root: string; branch: BranchState; files: FileChange[]; inProgress: OperationInProgress }
export type RepoState = { kind: 'repository'; status: RepoStatus } | { kind: 'not_repository' } | { kind: 'git_missing' }

export interface DiffLine { kind: 'context' | 'add' | 'delete'; text: string; oldNumber: number | null; newNumber: number | null; noNewlineAtEnd: boolean }
export interface DiffHunk { header: string; oldStart: number; oldLines: number; newStart: number; newLines: number; lines: DiffLine[] }
interface DiffBase { path: string; oldPath: string | null; oldMode: string | null; newMode: string | null; hash: string }
export type FileDiff =
  | (DiffBase & { kind: 'text'; hunks: DiffHunk[] })
  | (DiffBase & { kind: 'binary' })
  | (DiffBase & { kind: 'too_large'; bytes: number })
  | (DiffBase & { kind: 'empty' }) // a mode-only or rename-only change
```
- `DiffLine.text` is the line exactly as git printed it, without the leading marker and the newline. A trailing `\r` stays so that sprint 3 can rebuild a byte-exact patch from it. The view hides it.
- `hash` is the SHA-1 of the raw diff output (`node:crypto`). Sprint 3 uses it to check that a line selection still matches the file.

**State** (`src/main/git/status.ts`)
- `readRepoState(runner, folder): Promise<RepoState>`.
- Finding the repository:
  - `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` finds the root;
  - a folder outside any repository is `not_repository`, and `git_not_found` becomes `git_missing`;
  - a tracked folder may be a subfolder: report the repository root and run later commands there.
- Reading status:
  - run `git status --porcelain=v2 --branch -z --untracked-files=all --find-renames`;
  - parse it with a pure `parseStatusV2(output)`;
  - unmerged (`u`) entries become `conflicted`;
  - sort files by path.
- `inProgress`: check the paths that `git rev-parse --git-path <name>` gives for `MERGE_HEAD`, `rebase-merge`, `rebase-apply`, `CHERRY_PICK_HEAD` and `REVERT_HEAD`.
- The index is deliberately not exposed. As in GitHub Desktop, the change set is the working tree compared with HEAD.

**Diff** (`src/main/git/diffParser.ts`, `src/main/git/diff.ts`)
- A pure `parseUnifiedDiff(raw: string): FileDiff` parses one file's diff. It handles:
  - hunk headers and `\ No newline at end of file`;
  - `Binary files … differ`;
  - rename and copy headers;
  - `old mode`, `new mode`, `new file mode` and `deleted file mode`;
  - CRLF content.
- `readWorkingDiff(runner, root, change: FileChange, options?: { force?: boolean }): Promise<FileDiff>`:
  - for untracked files, and every file on an unborn branch, it runs `git diff --no-index --no-ext-diff --no-textconv --no-color -- /dev/null <path>`. Exit code 1 means "differences", not failure;
  - otherwise it runs `git diff --no-ext-diff --no-textconv --no-color --find-renames HEAD -- [<oldPath>] <path>`;
  - output over 2 MiB (16 MiB with `force`) becomes `too_large`, with the limit as `bytes`. Use the runner's `maxOutputBytes`.

**Out of scope**: IPC and UI.

**Verify** (write the tests first)
- Parser unit tests on fixture strings cover every header and line kind.
- `status.test.ts` and `diff.test.ts` run on real temp repositories (`src/test/gitRepo.ts`) and cover:
  - modified, added, deleted, untracked and binary (PNG bytes) files;
  - a rename (`git mv` plus an edit);
  - a typechange where the platform allows it (skip it with a note on Windows);
  - a file without a final newline, and a CRLF file whose lines keep `\r`;
  - a non-ASCII file name;
  - an unborn repository, a detached HEAD and a merge conflict between two branches;
  - a subfolder of a repository and a plain folder;
  - an upstream that is both ahead and behind (local bare remote).
- External programs: set `diff.external` and a `textconv` driver to scripts that write a marker file, read diffs, and assert that no marker exists.
- Run the touched tests, lint and typecheck.

Size: **medium**. This is a read-only diff viewer, used by Changes, by History and, in sprint 3, by line selection. It needs only the `FileDiff` type from `src/shared/git/diff.ts`.

**Component** (`src/renderer/src/source/DiffView.tsx`)
- Props: `{ diff: FileDiff | null; loading: boolean; error: string | null; onShowLarge?(): void }`.
- Keep the line-number gutter in its own component (`DiffGutter`), because sprint 3 adds line checkboxes there.
- A unified view, as in GitHub Desktop:
  - old and new line-number columns;
  - a `+`/`-` marker column;
  - a hunk header row (`@@ -a,b +c,d @@ context`);
  - add, delete and context tints.
- Text: monospace (`--font-mono`) with `tab-size: 4`. Whitespace is preserved, a trailing `\r` is not shown, and a missing final newline gets a "No newline at end of file" marker.
- Long lines scroll horizontally inside the diff; the page never scrolls sideways.
- States:
  - no file selected (`diff === null`, not loading);
  - loading;
  - error;
  - `binary`: "Binary file changed";
  - `too_large`: "This diff is large (N MB)", with **Show anyway** calling `onShowLarge`;
  - `empty`: "No content changes: the file mode or name changed".
- Big diffs: render the first 2,000 lines and a **Show N more lines** button. Use no virtualization library.
- Accessibility: a table with `aria-label="Diff of <path>"`. Each changed line also has screen-reader text, such as "added line 12" or "removed line 9".

**Styling**
- Put styles in `src/renderer/src/source/source.css`, imported by the component. The CSP forbids inline `style` attributes.
- Add new `:root` tokens in `src/renderer/src/styles.css`: `--diff-add-bg`, `--diff-add-ink`, `--diff-del-bg`, `--diff-del-ink`, `--diff-hunk-bg` and `--diff-gutter-ink`. Follow `docs/design/palette.md`, and add the tokens to the contrast tests (`theme.contrast.test.ts`).

**Out of scope**: fetching diffs, selection, a split view and syntax highlighting.

**Verify** (write the tests first)
- `DiffView.test.tsx` (jsdom) covers:
  - the line numbers of a two-hunk diff;
  - every state;
  - the no-newline marker and the hidden `\r`;
  - the 2,000-line cut and Show more.
- Run the token contrast tests.
- Run the touched tests, lint and typecheck. The acceptance ticket takes the screenshot once the view is mounted in the app.

acceptanceCriteria.text:
For a repository:
- the toolbar shows the branch, or the detached or unborn state;
- the Changes list shows each file with its status badge;
- selecting a file shows its diff;
- the list refreshes on window focus and every 5 s.

tickets.body:
Size: **medium**. Clicking a folder opens a folder page with **Source control** and **Epics** tabs, and Source control shows the repository's changes with their diffs. This ticket requires the bridge (`window.git`) and `DiffView`.

**Routing** (`src/renderer/src/app/`)
- `chooseView.ts`: replace the `home` and `onboarding` kinds with `{ kind: 'folder'; folder: TrackedFolderView; tab: FolderTab }`, where `FolderTab = 'source' | 'epics'`. The `loading`, `welcome`, `unavailable` and `epic` kinds stay.
- Tab memory:
  - store a `dm.folderTabs` localStorage map, `{ [folderPath]: FolderTab }`, through `usePersistentState`, with a guard like `isSelection`;
  - the default is `'source'`, and an unknown stored value falls back to it.
- Clicking a folder row (`selectFolder`, `shellActions.ts:82-85`) opens the folder page on its remembered tab. Opening an epic still shows the epic workspace.
- `App.tsx` (`MainPane` and `FolderPane`, about lines 70-117) renders a new `src/renderer/src/folder/FolderPage.tsx`, which has:
  - the folder header (eyebrow FOLDER, name, display path), moved out of `home/FolderHome.tsx`;
  - a tab strip with `role="tablist"` and arrow-key navigation, reusing the `.tp-tabs` pattern (`ticket/TicketPanel.tsx:65-82`);
  - the panel for the chosen tab: Source control; or, for Epics, the folder home body (with New epic) when the folder is initialized and `OnboardingView` when it isn't.
- `ShellFooter`'s `folderReady` becomes "a folder page or epic of an initialized folder".
- Update the existing tests that rely on `home` and `onboarding`: `chooseView.test.ts`, `MainViews.test.tsx`, `FolderHome.test.tsx` and the `App.*.test.tsx` files.

**Source control panel** (`src/renderer/src/source/`)
- `useRepoState(folder)` loads `window.git.getState` through `callGit` and drops stale responses (the `useResource` pattern). It refreshes:
  - every 5 s while mounted and the window is focused (`useRefreshTick`);
  - on the window `focus` event;
  - on `refresh()`.
- `SourceControlView.tsx` shows these states:
  - loading;
  - `git_missing`: "Git isn't installed", with a link to https://git-scm.com/downloads through `window.dm.openExternal`;
  - `not_repository`: "This folder isn't a Git repository", with **Initialize repository** (`initRepository`), and then the empty repository;
  - error, with Retry.
- A repository shows:
  - a toolbar with the branch name (or "Detached HEAD at <short oid>", or "No commits yet"), and the repository root when it differs from the folder;
  - a 320 px left column titled **Changes (N)**. Each file row shows the directory dimmed, the file name bold, a status badge (A, M, D, R, U, ?, or ! for conflicted) and, for renames, the old path. A clean repository shows "No local changes";
  - a right column with `DiffView` for the selected file, loaded with `getWorkingDiff`. Show anyway passes `force`. The selection survives refreshes while the file is still listed.

**Out of scope**: checkboxes, commit and discard (the next ticket), and History.

**Verify** (write the tests first)
- Tests:
  - `chooseView` and tab memory;
  - `FolderPage` tabs and keyboard navigation;
  - each `SourceControlView` state, with `FakeGit`;
  - refresh on focus and on the timer, with `__mocks__/manualScheduler.ts`.
- Take a screenshot of this repository's Source control tab with a changed file's diff open, from the built app with an isolated profile.
- Run the touched tests (including the updated ones), lint and typecheck.

acceptanceCriteria.text:
In `scratch-b`, the app:
1. creates a branch from the default branch;
2. switches away, leaving changes stashed;
3. comes back and restores the changes;
4. renames the branch;
5. deletes it together with its remote branch.

After each step, `git branch -a` and `git stash list` in a terminal match what the app shows.

Starting sign-in:
- returns a user code and a verification URL, and opens that URL in the browser;
- polls in a way that honours `authorization_pending` and `slow_down`;
- on success, stores the account and broadcasts it.

Expiry, denial, a misconfigured app and cancel each end the attempt with their own code. Tests use a fake fetch and clock.

Merging a branch into the current one either merges or returns `merge_conflicts`. A DM stash can be:
- listed with its files;
- restored, which returns `merge_conflicts` on a conflict and keeps the stash;
- discarded.

tickets.body:
Size: **medium**. Cloning from the sidebar. This ticket requires the clone operations.

**Entry points**
- The sidebar **+** (`src/renderer/src/sidebar/Sidebar.tsx:57`) opens a `Menu` with **Add existing folder…** (today's track flow) and **Clone repository…**.
- `WelcomeView` (`app/MainViews.tsx`) gets a **Clone repository** button beside Choose folder.

**Dialog** (`src/renderer/src/clone/CloneDialog.tsx`)
- It has two tabs:
  - **GitHub.com**: signed out, it shows `SignInPrompt` ("Sign in to GitHub to see your repositories"). Signed in, it shows a filterable list of the account's repositories grouped by owner, with a lock icon for private ones, a fork label, and **Refresh**;
  - **URL**: an input for a URL or `owner/repo`.
- **Local path**:
  - the parent folder comes from `getCloneParent`, and **Choose…** calls `chooseCloneParent`;
  - a **Name** field defaults to the repository's name;
  - the full target path is shown.
- **Clone** runs `clone` with a new `operationId`. The dialog then shows a progress bar with the phase and percent, and **Cancel**.
- Success closes the dialog, selects the new folder in the sidebar and opens its Source control tab.
- Errors show inline:
  - `auth_required` or `auth_failed`: `SignInPrompt`;
  - a target that isn't empty: "<path> already exists";
  - anything else: the message, with git's detail.

**Verify** (write the tests first, with `FakeGit`, `FakeGithub` and `FakeDm`)
- Tests:
  - the + menu;
  - both tabs, filtering and the signed-out prompt;
  - the target path;
  - progress and cancel;
  - success selecting the folder on Source control;
  - each error.
- Screenshots from the built app with an isolated profile: the dialog's GitHub.com tab while signed out, and the URL tab during a clone of a public repository (for example https://github.com/octocat/Hello-World).
- Run the touched tests, lint and typecheck.

Size: **medium**. Commit only some lines of a file, as GitHub Desktop does. This ticket is the main side only; the next ticket adds the UI. Its one hard part: the patch must be exact.

**Patch builder** (`src/main/git/partialPatch.ts`, pure)
- `buildPartialPatch(diff: Extract<FileDiff, { kind: 'text' }>, selected: ReadonlySet<number>): string | null`.
- `selected` holds indices of the diff's changed lines: `add` and `delete` lines only, counted in order across hunks. Context lines have no index. Export this indexing as `changedLineIndices(diff)` from `src/shared/git/diff.ts`, so the renderer uses the same numbering.
- For each hunk:
  - a selected `add` line stays `+`, and an unselected `add` line is dropped;
  - a selected `delete` line stays `-`, and an unselected `delete` line becomes context (` `);
  - context stays context;
  - recompute `oldLines` and `newLines`, and shift `newStart` by the running offset of earlier hunks;
  - drop hunks with no selected change.
- A `\ No newline at end of file` marker follows the line it belongs to, including when that line becomes context.
- Headers:
  - `diff --git a/<old> b/<new>`;
  - mode lines from `oldMode` and `newMode`;
  - `rename from` and `rename to` for renames;
  - `--- /dev/null` and `new file mode` for new files.
- A partially selected deleted file becomes a modification that keeps the unselected lines. A partially selected new file is created with only the selected lines.
- Write each line byte-exact from `DiffLine.text`, a trailing `\r` included. With nothing selected, return `null`. Binary diffs are not accepted.

**Commit with lines** (`src/main/git/commit.ts`, `GitApi.commit`)
- `files` entries gain `lines?: number[]` and `diffHash?: string`.
- For an entry with `lines`:
  1. read the file's current working diff (`readWorkingDiff`). If its `hash` differs from `diffHash`, return `stale_selection` (add this code) and commit nothing;
  2. after the index reset, apply `buildPartialPatch` with `git apply --cached --whitespace=nowarn -` (the patch on stdin), instead of `git add`.
- Entries without `lines` are staged whole, as today. The working tree is never changed.

**Verify** (write the tests first, on real temp repositories)
- After each commit, assert `git show HEAD:<path>` and that the working file is unchanged.
- Cases:
  - selected adds only, and selected deletes only;
  - mixed lines in one hunk;
  - several hunks, where an earlier hunk's selection shifts the later ones;
  - a new file partly selected, and a deleted file partly selected;
  - no final newline on either side;
  - a CRLF file;
  - a renamed file with part of its edit;
  - a mode change kept.
- Selecting every line gives the same tree as committing the whole file. Selecting none returns `null`. A stale `diffHash` returns `stale_selection`.
- Run the touched tests, lint and typecheck.

Size: **medium**. Choose lines and hunks to commit in the diff, as in GitHub Desktop. This ticket requires the partial commit in main.

**DiffView** (`src/renderer/src/source/DiffView.tsx`, `DiffGutter`)
- New optional prop: `selection?: { selected: ReadonlySet<number>; onToggle(indices: number[], include: boolean): void }`. It uses `changedLineIndices` from `src/shared/git/diff.ts`.
- With `selection`:
  - each changed line's gutter shows its checkbox state;
  - clicking a gutter toggles the line;
  - dragging across gutters sets the whole range to the toggled state of the first line;
  - clicking a hunk header's gutter toggles the whole hunk;
  - Space toggles the focused line.
- Unselected changed lines are dimmed. History diffs pass no `selection` and stay read-only.

**Inclusion** (`useInclusion.ts`, `ChangesPanel.tsx`)
- Each file is `all`, `none` or `partial(set)`. The file checkbox is indeterminate for partial, and clicking it toggles all or none.
- A partial selection is kept while the file's diff `hash` is unchanged. When the hash changes, the file resets to all, and a toast says "<file> changed, so its line selection was reset".
- Commit sends `lines` and `diffHash` for partial files. `stale_selection` refreshes the diff and shows the same toast.
- The header still reads "N changed files", and the commit button stays enabled while at least one file is partly included.

**Verify** (write the tests first, with `FakeGit`)
- Tests:
  - line, range-drag, hunk and keyboard toggles, and the dimming;
  - the tri-state file checkbox;
  - the reset when the hash changes;
  - the commit payload with lines and hash, and `stale_selection` handling;
  - History diffs not selectable.
- Take a screenshot of a diff with some lines unselected and the file checkbox indeterminate, from the built app with an isolated profile.
- Run the touched tests, lint and typecheck.

Size: **small**. Documents what the epic built. It runs after the clone, pull request and line selection tickets, so it describes what landed. Read their accepted results and the code before writing.

- **Decision record**: `docs/decisions/0002-source-control-in-main.md` (use the next free number if 0002 is taken), in the style of `0001-sqlite-driver.md`. Record:
  - person-initiated git writes live in `src/main/git` and `src/main/github`, behind `window.git` and `window.github`, outside core and MCP, and core's adapter stays read-only;
  - the change model: the working tree compared with HEAD;
  - pull only merges;
  - discard moves content to the trash;
  - automatic reads disable fsmonitor, external diff and textconv, while commits run hooks;
  - the device flow, the `safeStorage` token, and the environment-based credential helper scoped to `https://github.com`.
- **`docs/architecture.md`**:
  - add the two bridges and the `src/main/git` and `src/main/github` modules to the process chain and the module list;
  - reword the read-only git note (around lines 111-115) to say that core never writes to git, while the desktop's Source control does on the person's request.
- **`docs/product-plan.md:152`**: automatic commits and pushes stay out of scope; person-initiated ones through Source control are in.
- **`docs/runbooks/github-oauth-app.md`**:
  - how to register the GitHub OAuth App: github.com → Settings → Developer settings → OAuth Apps → New. Give a name and a homepage URL, any callback URL (the device flow doesn't use it), and tick **Enable Device Flow**;
  - where the client ID lives (`src/main/github/config.ts`);
  - how to rotate it.
- **`README.md`**: a Source control section covering:
  - what it does;
  - that it needs git on PATH;
  - signing in, and where the token is kept;
  - that sign-out doesn't revoke the grant; Manage access on GitHub does.

**Verify**
- Every file path and command named in the docs exists; check with a search.
- Links between docs resolve.
- `npm run lint` is unaffected, because this ticket changes docs only.
